ent-SunriseMechReactorStandard = standard mech reactor
    .desc = A compact reactor with modest cooling and a long recovery cycle.

ent-SunriseMechReactorWorkhorse = workhorse-class reactor
    .desc = A reinforced reactor with additional heat capacity, designed for sustained operation.

ent-SunriseMechReactorDurandale = durandale-class reactor
    .desc = A reinforced reactor designed exclusively for DURAND-class mechs. Its integrated BR-40c "Turtle" energy barrier consumes very little power while idle. The shield is activated using a signal transmitter.

ent-SunriseMechReactorRoland = roland-class reactor
    .desc = A reinforced reactor designed exclusively for DURAND-class mechs. Its integrated blood-red energy barrier consumes very little power while idle. The shield is activated using a signal transmitter.

ent-SunriseMechReactorLonghaul = longhaul-class reactor
    .desc = Deep heat sinks and an upgraded coolant loop allow this reactor to operate for extended periods.

ent-SunriseMechReactorThor = thor-class reactor
    .desc = An advanced cooling system gives this reactor a short recovery cycle at the cost of heat capacity.

ent-SunriseMechReactorEmperor = emperor-class reactor
    .desc = An antique reactor from a more refined age. Its cooling system appears almost flawless.

ent-SunriseMechReactorPaladin = paladin-class reactor
    .desc = An antique reactor whose casing contains an integrated energy shield generator. The shield is activated using a signal transmitter.

ent-SunriseMechReactorBurnout = burnout-class reactor
    .desc = An oversized disposable reactor designed for an extreme burst of power. Its core cannot recover once depleted.

ent-SunriseMechReactorCavalier = cavalier-class reactor
    .desc = An overclocked reactor tuned for higher mech speed at the expense of heat capacity.
